# §9 B type overload by arity + self { … } construction
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (docs/design/plano-secao9B-type-overload.md — the 8-crumb plan):
#   - RE-KEY THE TYPE-DECL REGISTRY, in `src/checker/collect.tks`. `duplicates_of_reg` adds the arity
#     (`decl.type_params.len`) to the collision key; the diagnostic names it (`duplicate type 'Foo'
#     (arity N) in namespace '…'`). Same-arity is a duplicate regardless of constraint OR type-param
#     name; cross-kind (struct/enum/class) collides through the same key.
#   - ARITY-SELECTIVE RESOLUTION, in `src/checker/resolve.tks`. A new `type_table_find_arity` and an
#     `arity` parameter threaded through `resolve_named` / `resolve_type_ref` / `resolve_type_reg` /
#     `resolve_bare_type_reg` / `resolve_qualified_type_reg` / `resolve_root_scope_reg`, from the
#     `resolve_type` entry points (bare = arity 0, `Foo<A..>` = `nt.args.len`). A bare reference to a
#     name that exists only as a generic is a diagnosed error (`names a generic type — write Foo<…>`);
#     the arity-count refinement for `Foo<A..>` migrates to `generic_inst_arity_error`.
#   - `self { … }` PARSING, in `src/parser/parse_expr.tks`. A `{` after `self` (when struct literals
#     are allowed) parses a construction via `parse_struct_lit` with a single-segment `self` sentinel
#     path (`self_sentinel_path`) — no new AST field, `.tkb` shape unchanged.
#   - CONSTRUCTION REWRITE, in `src/checker/typer.tks`. `type_struct_lit` dispatches its prefix
#     (`construct_target`): `self { … }` (`self_construct_target`, resolving `env.owner_type`,
#     phantom-stamped for a generic owner), `Foo<A..> { … }` (`explicit_inst_target`) and bare
#     `Foo { … }` (`bare_construct_target`, arity 0, never borrowing arity from `expected`). The
#     annotation-retarget of a bare generic and the `is_self_generic_construct` inference are DELETED.
#   - PHANTOM SELF SPELLING KEPT, single-sourced. `phantom_self_inst_name` is RENAMED to the neutral
#     `self_inst_spelling` (NOT deleted): its second consumer `instance_method_subst_l5`
#     (`src/checker/monomorph.tks`) needs the phantom→instance remap spelling, so the string stays
#     single-sourced and shared by the `self` construction branch and the mono remap.
#   - PRODUCT SWEEP. `List<T>::make` and `Map<V>::make` construct via `self { … }` instead of the
#     deleted bare-`List{}`/`Map{}`-is-Self inference — behavior-preserving (same phantom name, same
#     template decl, same TStructInit).
# WHAT DOES NOT ENTER: no method/function overload (that is §9 A) and no defaults/named args (§9 C);
# `self { … }` takes no explicit type-args (Self's arity comes from the enclosing type); no `.tkb`
# format change (arity is `type_params.len`, derived, never persisted).
#
# INERTNESS OF THE RE-KEY/ARITY PARTS. Every current type name has exactly ONE arity, so a `Foo`/
# `Foo<T>` pair (which would collide under today's keyless `(ns,name)`) does not exist; the arity key
# gives the same 0-duplicate verdict and the arity-selective resolvers return the same single
# registration `type_table_find` returned. The ONLY source whose spelling changed is the two-site
# self-construct sweep, and its typed output is identical (proven by the ACCEPT fixture round-tripping
# the same generic-class + `self { … }` static/instance pattern on both backends).
